# Docs notebook conventions

`app/notebooks/<id>.notebook.yaml` is the notebook; `app/notebooks/<id>.md` is its
sidecar of collapsible "[more]" explanations. These are auto-discovered and solved
by `app/scripts/build-notebook-data.mjs` — they are **not** moneyjs pilot templates,
so the submodule's `compile:notebook-yaml` does not apply. Never edit `moneyjs/` or
the generated `app/src/data/`.

## Sidecar markers

Each panel starts with a marker on its own line; text runs until the next marker:

```
<!-- more: <cellId> -->
```

- `<cellId>` must match a cell `id` in the YAML (unknown ids are skipped with a
  warning); one block per id, last wins.

## Rendering: no KaTeX

Panels render via `AssistantMarkdown` (no `remark-math`). Use backticks, not LaTeX:

- ✅ `` `Y = Cs + Gs` `` and `` `alpha1` ``
- ❌ `$Y = C_s + G_s$`
- Use `pow(b, e)`, never `^`, for exponentiation.

## Cells & scenarios

- One wrapper key per cell (`markdown`/`matrix`/`run`/`chart`/`table`/…); no `type`.
- `chart`/`table` `variables` are bare model variable names, not expressions.
- Scenario runs start from the baseline's last-period state; shocks (`constant` or
  `series`) apply over `rangeInclusive` and target **externals** only. A `series`
  maps `values[period - start]`. For growth, drive an external with a geometric
  `series`.

## Validation

Run `pnpm build:data` (solves every notebook — watch for `unknown cell id` and
`failed to solve` warnings), then `pnpm test`. `pnpm typecheck` currently fails on
pre-existing submodule errors, so it is not a reliable gate for notebook changes.
